      "description": "Watch Al Hilal Saudi FC vs Al Ahli Jeddah highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 1, 2026. The Pro League spotlight turned to a massive encounter on September 1, 2026, as Al Hilal Saudi FC and Al Ahli Jeddah prepared to face off in a highly anticipated fixture. Fans expected drama from the opening whistle, and the two giants of Saudi football did not disappoint in a game defined by tactical intensity. Early Breakthrough for Al Hilal The match burst into life early on as Al Hilal Saudi FC looked to assert their dominance. In the 9th minute, the deadlock was broken when Sultan Mandash delivered a precise ball for Sergej Milinkovic-Savic , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. The momentum stayed with the home side, and by the 23rd minute, they had doubled their advantage. Ruben Neves turned provider, setting up Crysencio Summerville for a clinical finish that left Al Ahli Jeddah reeling under the pressure. Discipline Crumbles Before the Break As the first half drew to a close, the temperature of the match reached a boiling point. A flurry of bookings saw Roger Ibanez , Mohamed Meite , and Crysencio Summerville all enter the referee's book as tackles flew in. However, the biggest flashpoint occurred deep in stoppage time. Following a heated exchange that saw both Ivan Toney and Merih Demiral cautioned, the situation escalated. In the 45+7th minute, Merih Demiral was shown a straight red card, leaving his team a man down and sparking furious protests from the Al Ahli players and staff. Tactical Shifts and the Final Blow The second half began with a raft of tactical changes as both managers looked to adapt to the new dynamics of the ten-man contest. Al Hilal introduced Ollie Watkins for Mohamed Meite at the restart to maintain their offensive edge. Despite the numerical disadvantage, Al Ahli fought to stay in the contest, but the pressure eventually told in the closing stages. In the 86th minute, Sultan Mandash capped off a brilliant individual performance with his second assist of the night, picking out Ollie Watkins who fired home to put the result beyond doubt and secure all three points."
